2) the ceiling this retrieval puts on any scorer, against what the study got
   rag, floor as shipped        ceiling rho +0.732 tau +0.623 (distinct 14, MAE 16.03) | Q4_K_M +0.721 / MAE 24.80, no-LLM +0.299 / MAE 55.30 on these same 30
   rag, floor 0.0 (no filter)   ceiling rho +0.721 tau +0.626 (distinct 13, MAE 14.73) | Q4_K_M +0.721 / MAE 24.80, no-LLM +0.299 / MAE 55.30 on these same 30
   rag, shipped floor, no cap   ceiling rho +0.975 tau +0.930 (distinct 15, MAE 3.13) | Q4_K_M +0.721 / MAE 24.80, no-LLM +0.299 / MAE 55.30 on these same 30
   full context (reference)     ceiling rho +1.000 tau +1.000 (distinct 13, MAE 0.00) | Q4_K_M +0.721 / MAE 24.80, no-LLM +0.299 / MAE 55.30 on these same 30
   the ceiling is not a model result: it is the rubric applied to what the retriever
   delivered, so it bounds any reader of that block. Splitting the shortfall on these 30:
   +0.268 rho is the evidence's (1.000 -> +0.732) and +0.011 is the model's
   (+0.732 -> +0.721). On MAE the model gives away more: 16.03 for a
   faithful reader of the same block against 24.80 measured.

